# Copy to .env (or .env.production) and fill in before `npm run build` for a
# real deployment. See README.md's Configuration section.

# Base URL of the platform API. Leave unset for same-origin.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://rwa.example.com

# sumsub or onfido. Leave unset when the deployment has no KYC provider.
# VITE_KYC_PROVIDER=

# --- Pinned deployment addresses --------------------------------------------
#
# This deployment's own program ids and mints, baked into the build.
# Every buy/redemption/transfer instruction hard-asserts the equivalent
# value it receives at runtime from GET /api/v1/config and GET /api/v1/project
# against these pins before it will build a transaction, and refuses (throws)
# on any mismatch. This is what actually delivers the "a compromised server
# can't redirect an on-chain action" property for this deployment — without
# these set, every program id/mint is trusted from the server unverified, and
# the app shows a visible warning banner.
#
# VITE_SOLANA_PROGRAM_COMPLIANCE=
# VITE_SOLANA_PROGRAM_VAULT=
# VITE_SOLANA_PROGRAM_PRICING=
# VITE_SOLANA_PROGRAM_TRANSFER_HOOK=
# VITE_SOLANA_PROGRAM_REDEMPTION=
# VITE_SOLANA_PROGRAM_SUPPLY_CONTROLLER=
# VITE_SOLANA_RWA_MINT=
# VITE_SOLANA_QUOTE_MINT=

# --- Pinned RPC endpoint -----------------------------------------------------
#
# The RPC node every read AND write in this app goes through, and
# part of the same trust boundary as the program id/mint pins above:
# GET /api/v1/project no longer returns an RPC endpoint at all, so this
# build-time value is the ONLY source. Leaving it unset in a real deployment
# silently falls back to a local-validator default (http://127.0.0.1:8899)
# — harmless in dev, useless in production — so treat it as required in
# practice even though nothing enforces that at build time; the app's own
# warning banner (pinsConfigured) flags a build that shipped
# without it. Historically the server supplied Project.publicRpcUrl
# and this pin only had to catch a compromised server redirecting reads
# through it; that field has since been removed from the API entirely, since
# a build-time pin makes a server-supplied value redundant for this purpose.
#
# This value is ALSO baked into the build's Content-Security-Policy
# connect-src (see vite.config.ts / src/lib/cspPolicy.ts) — every
# @solana/web3.js Connection call is an ordinary same-page fetch(). Leaving
# it unset ships a build that cannot make any RPC call in production.
#
# A NON-loopback endpoint MUST be https:// (see VITE_SOLANA_WS_URL's note
# below for why — the same rule applies here).
#
# VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL=

# The Connection's WebSocket transport endpoint — used
# by confirmTransaction/account subscriptions. web3.js derives one from
# VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL when this is left unset (swapping the scheme and
# bumping the port by one), but that derived origin is NOT necessarily what
# gets baked into the CSP's connect-src above, so set this explicitly for any
# real deployment so the CSP allow-lists the exact origin the app opens.
#
# A NON-loopback endpoint MUST be wss://, not ws:// — this build's CSP also
# sends upgrade-insecure-requests, which browsers apply to ANY ws: source
# (not just loopback-exempt ones): a plain ws:// endpoint gets silently
# rewritten to wss:// and fails to connect, since the RPC node serves no TLS
# on that port. http://localhost:8899 / ws://localhost:8900 (or 127.0.0.1)
# are the only plain-http/ws origins the upgrade doesn't break.
#
# VITE_SOLANA_WS_URL=

# Optional: the pinned RPC endpoint's expected cluster genesis hash (base58).
# Cross-checked once per session (per RPC endpoint) via getGenesisHash() —
# catches a wrong-cluster endpoint (e.g. devnet instead of mainnet) that still
# looks like a plausible URL. Mirrors the equivalent server-side fix. Leave
# unset to skip this extra check (VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL above still applies).
#
# VITE_SOLANA_CLUSTER_GENESIS=
